35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The allocation is down a quarter, and off-site contacts earn nothing. We must build on-site to recoup costs.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth, then reversed. The shared round failed due to logistics. We need a program that actually sticks, not just another experiment.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The therapy review shows four years of physiotherapists leaving, while midwifery has unusual slack. We must balance this pressure before adding new duties.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The booking system hides unbooked work, and parking fills by eleven. We physically cannot absorb more patients without a major overhaul.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,Those minutes show the clinic collapsed when neither side owned the rota. The data agreements took fourteen months. We must avoid relying on outside bodies that never truly committed.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, your reversal data is critical. With the budget cut, we cannot afford failed experiments. We need a model that sustains itself financially and operationally.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Jonathan, the reversal proves fragility. We need structural change, not just funding. Midori, your staffing data confirms the operational bottleneck.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"Thank you, Shion. I agree. With nine vacant posts and rising agency costs, we can’t just add tasks. We need a program that respects our current capacity.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, exactly. If parking is full and rooms are booked, adding more patients just creates chaos. We need a program that fits our current physical limits, not one that breaks them.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Kenji. We must choose a program that fits our current limits, not one that breaks them.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, your caution is wise. With the budget cut, we need a self-contained model. Does the midwifery slack offer a viable, low-cost starting point?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Midori, that midwifery slack is a distraction. We need to fix the broken discharge loop, not fill empty chairs. The data demands structural repair.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I hear your urgency, but ignoring the midwifery slack wastes a rare opportunity. We must use that capacity to support the discharge loop, not ignore it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, I agree with Midori. Using existing midwifery slack avoids adding new physical strain. It fits our current limits without breaking the booking system or parking.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, I agree. Using existing capacity is wise. We must ensure the midwifery team is truly willing to take this on, so it doesn’t crumble later.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Leveraging existing midwifery capacity minimizes new costs. We must ensure this model remains financially viable within our reduced allocation.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Midori, your point is valid. The slack is real, but it’s a resource, not a solution. We must integrate it into the discharge loop to prevent the reversal I saw.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I appreciate the compromise, Shion. Integrating midwifery into the discharge loop respects our staffing reality while addressing your data concerns. It feels like a balanced, sustainable path forward for everyone.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I’m glad we’re aligning. Using midwifery slack keeps the booking system calm and parking manageable. It fits our physical limits perfectly without causing a bottleneck.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I’m glad we’re finding common ground. I just want to gently ensure the midwifery team feels truly supported, so this doesn’t quietly unravel later.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
